1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,980
=Episode 4=

15
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:29,360
Yuyuan, I've come to apologize.

16
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:34,670
Good morning,

17
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:36,210
Xiang.

18
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:40,160
And who are these people...

19
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:43,640
Well, you don't know, Xiang.

20
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,250
Lately,

21
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,240
I've been having dreams

22
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:48,220
about someone trying to poison me.

23
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,840
So I hired a group

24
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,020
of experienced food tasters.

25
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:55,740
Is that bowl of soup

26
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:57,920
for me?

27
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,200
Bring it over. I'd love to try it.

28
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,400
Let me taste it first.

29
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:25,640
Goodness, what a bunch of hungry girls.

30
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,240
Xiang worked so hard

31
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,100
to make this soup with love,

32
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,100
and you've tasted every last drop.

33
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,700
Sorry about that, Xiang.

34
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:35,950
Do you have any more?

35
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:36,760
You...

36
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:38,880
I...

37
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,710
I'll come back another time.

38
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:42,640
Hmph.

39
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:44,320
- Hmph.
- Hmph.

40
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,040
Hmph.

41
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,710
(Next,)

42
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,230
(the musk infertility scheme.)

43
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:51,790
Here.

44
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,550
If I can't poison you to death,

45
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,640
I'll make sure you can't have children.

46
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:01,830
Let's go.

47
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,960
Search the area within five li

48
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,760
of my courtyard

49
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,270
and the Heir's wife.

50
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:11,670
Turn the place upside down,

51
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,080
and hand over anything you find

52
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,830
that isn't soil.

53
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,090
- Yes.
- Yes.

54
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:38,440
Shutiao,

55
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:40,080
stop shaking it.

56
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:40,600
Stop it.

57
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:43,270
You've been avoiding me
these past few days.

58
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,110
Let's see where you can run this time.

59
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,260
Oh, dear my sisters-in-law.

60
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,330
I know I've made mistakes,

61
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:50,120
but you can't

62
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,660
keep picking on me.

63
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,950
Stay back.

64
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:53,590
No.

65
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:54,590
Don't push me.

66
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:00,770
- Madam.
- Madam.

67
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,640
- No...
- No...

68
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,310
What was that just now?

69
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:23,200
Don't be afraid, Xiang.

70
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:24,190
They're all part of

71
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:24,750
my specially

72
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:26,440
hired underwater rescue team.

73
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:27,750
They specialize in handling

74
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:28,680
all kinds of accidental falls into water

75
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,030
caused by slips and stumbles.

76
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,900
They're available whenever
you need them.

77
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:34,800
By the way,

78
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,430
their wages were all paid for

79
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:36,800
with the musk

80
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,160
you buried, Xiang.

81
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,350
Isn't that a great deal?

82
00:04:45,070 --> 00:04:46,160
There's still plenty of money left

83
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,410
from selling the musk.

84
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,560
Where did you hide it?

85
00:04:56,190 --> 00:04:56,680
Don't move.

86
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:08,750
♪Fallen leaves gently ripple the water♪

87
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,940
♪A soft breeze brushes
through your hair♪

88
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,440
Do you usually read

89
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,900
such explicit books?

90
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,140
(The Book of Human Anatomy)

91
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,120
So you pretend to be a playboy

92
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,270
to hide your study
of forensic examination?

93
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:37,750
Then why did you

94
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:38,770
drug me on our wedding night?

95
00:05:40,190 --> 00:05:40,920
Because I was afraid

96
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,830
you'd try something with me.

97
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:43,630
Besides, what I gave you

98
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:44,830
was just a drug that causes rashes.

99
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,590
I only wanted to scare you.

100
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:49,800
Who knew...

101
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:53,150
Anyway,

102
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:54,510
you've discovered my secret now.

103
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:55,800
If you want to report me,

104
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:56,920
go tell Grandmother.

105
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,200
What's there to report?

106
00:05:59,070 --> 00:05:59,710
A coroner

107
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,060
seeks justice for the living

108
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,030
and speaks for the dead.

109
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,390
It's an honest profession
that takes real skill.

110
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,640
Why act like you
are doing something wrong?

111
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:09,760
You...

112
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,470
You don't look down on me for this?

113
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,190
Strictly speaking,

114
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:15,660
we're in the same line of work.

115
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,600
You speak for the dead,

116
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,180
and I save the living.

117
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,000
(The Book of Human Anatomy)
But this book is outdated.

118
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:23,000
Look.

119
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:24,950
(Cinnabar: Sweet, slightly cold)
A child's heart and lungs

120
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:26,080
are closer than an adult's.

121
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:27,870
So the location of internal organ damage

122
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:30,000
should be three parts lower.

123
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,080
I see.

124
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,640
No wonder I kept getting it wrong.

125
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:35,980
You really know this stuff.

126
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:37,320
Could you teach me?

127
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,430
You'll have to pay some tuition first.

128
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:48,590
What are you doing?

129
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,560
I'm a traditional man.

130
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:57,560
If you want to get intimate,

131
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:58,910
we need to take things
one step at a time.

132
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:00,910
Don't get carried away.

133
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:01,760
Come here.

134
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,760
Watch closely.

135
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,470
In adults, the heart
and lungs are this far apart.

136
00:07:24,290 --> 00:07:27,870
♪Watching drifting clouds cross
the green mountains♪

137
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:31,600
♪Side by side, we hear
the evening breeze softly sigh♪

138
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:35,250
♪Through countless years
of everyday joys♪

139
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:39,780
♪I'm blessed to have you
by my side in this life♪

140
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:45,360
When it really matters,

141
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:47,290
you need something that holds its value.

142
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,430
It'll be easier to flee with, too.

143
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:51,470
Where are you planning to go?

144
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:57,660
Your Lordship,

145
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,480
what brings you here?

146
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:01,330
Surely

147
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:03,440
it's not time
for another blood donation yet?

148
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:05,440
My blood may be good,

149
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:07,790
but you shouldn't take too much.

150
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,430
First Madam has been

151
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:10,560
causing quite a bit of trouble lately.

152
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,690
If your wife is unhappy,

153
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,430
the quality of her blood might suffer.

154
00:08:15,350 --> 00:08:15,990
Why don't

155
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:16,990
you buy her a gift

156
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:17,840
to cheer her up?

157
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,240
I can't bring myself

158
00:08:19,950 --> 00:08:20,640
to please someone else.

159
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:25,610
You got me a gift?

160
00:08:25,830 --> 00:08:26,860
This necklace

161
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,710
is made from materials
I collected myself.

162
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,920
You collected them yourself?

163
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,720
But why can't I tell

164
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,040
what it's made of?

165
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,690
I must not have

166
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:38,710
seen enough of the world.

167
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,530
Could it be ivory?

168
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:43,360
This

169
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,140
is far more valuable than ivory.

170
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,320
This was made

171
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:49,080
from the finger bones

172
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:50,940
I broke off, one by one,

173
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,440
from heinous criminals

174
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,630
sentenced to death over the years.

175
00:08:58,060 --> 00:08:58,910
You're that excited?

176
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:01,990
Next time,

177
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,420
I'll take you to the prison

178
00:09:03,670 --> 00:09:04,750
and let you make a set yourself.

179
00:09:07,030 --> 00:09:08,030
(Make it myself?)

180
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:08,990
(How is this a gift?)

181
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,920
(It's an outright threat.)

182
00:09:12,670 --> 00:09:13,400
There's no need.

183
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,750
I'm hardly worthy

184
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:17,710
of wearing so many
distinguished predecessors.

185
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,830
You should keep it, Your Lordship.

186
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,240
I have something to attend to,

187
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,320
so I'll be going now.

188
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:27,720
(Come on, legs.)

189
00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:29,220
(Move.)

190
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,400
Sanqi was right after all.

191
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:35,970
She's so delighted

192
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,100
she can barely walk straight.

193
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,870
(Shen Manor)

194
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:39,590
Xiang,

195
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:44,820
I've finished sorting out

196
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,080
the estate accounts for you.

197
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,060
But I haven't seen you in a few days.

198
00:09:48,790 --> 00:09:49,800
What's wrong?

199
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,150
It's all because of those two wretches

200
00:09:52,150 --> 00:09:53,280
from the second and third branches.

201
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:55,280
I married a concubine's son
who died young.

202
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,490
I've spent all these years
being careful,

203
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:58,510
and finally managed

204
00:09:58,510 --> 00:09:59,360
to win Grandmother's favor

205
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,230
and take charge of the household.

206
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:02,150
Who knew they

207
00:10:02,150 --> 00:10:03,120
would be so cunning?

208
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:03,920
If only I hadn't...

209
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,470
I never should've listened to Xiangchun.

210
00:10:08,270 --> 00:10:09,040
Xiang,

211
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:11,710
you've managed
the Marquis's Manor for years.

212
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,560
Xiangchun was only looking out for you.

213
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:15,630
But now,

214
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:17,000
those two new sisters-in-law

215
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,110
have gained so much influence.

216
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,040
If you

217
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,160
really keep swallowing your pride,

218
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,150
I'm afraid that Bai

219
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:25,750
will have to

220
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:28,200
live at their mercy.

221
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,040
But I've

222
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,200
just been stripped
of my authority by Grandmother.

223
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,510
She even ordered me
to reflect on my mistakes.

224
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:37,350
If I cause any trouble now...

225
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:40,160
You needn't do anything yourself, Xiang.

226
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,040
In this household,

227
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,240
there are plenty of ways

228
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,330
to make them

229
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:46,080
fall in line.

230
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:47,340
You have a plan?

231
00:10:58,510 --> 00:10:59,750
The family banquet is coming up.

232
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:01,030
I

233
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:03,080
have arranged to have
two outfits made for you.

234
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,810
I'm sure you'll love them.

235
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,700
You know,

236
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,910
Xiang has been much quieter lately.

237
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:10,220
We can finally take it easy, right?

238
00:11:10,450 --> 00:11:11,160
Stop right there.

239
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:13,150
Whenever someone says that in a novel,

240
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,200
trouble is bound to follow.

241
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:14,950
Bad news.

242
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:15,670
Bad news,

243
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,270
Old Madam.

244
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,200
Something terrible has happened.

245
00:11:18,510 --> 00:11:19,470
What's the panic?

246
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:20,570
Take your time.

247
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:21,720
First Madam has fainted.

248
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,030
The manor summoned a Taoist master,

249
00:11:23,030 --> 00:11:23,470
who said she's...

250
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:24,870
She's possessed by an evil spirit.

251
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,560
What?

252
00:11:48,390 --> 00:11:49,440
Be careful, Grandmother.

253
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,400
First Madam remains unconscious

254
00:11:54,910 --> 00:11:55,870
because

255
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:57,040
one of her three souls
has left her body.

256
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:57,950
There must be an evil spirit

257
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,760
within the Marquis's Manor.

258
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:00,670
Master,

259
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:01,940
is there a way to resolve this?

260
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,880
Don't worry, Old Madam.

261
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:05,370
I'll summon lightning

262
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:07,350
to reveal the evil spirit.

263
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:09,040
Tell me,

264
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:11,480
we haven't seen Xiang in quite a while.

265
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,400
You don't think
they'll blame us, do you?

266
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:15,160
Who knows?

267
00:12:21,390 --> 00:12:22,280
What is that?

268
00:12:23,030 --> 00:12:23,830
Found it.

269
00:12:24,630 --> 00:12:25,510
It's you two.

270
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:32,180
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

271
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:39,380
♪Right now,
I just want to stay by your side♪

272
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:44,580
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

273
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:50,820
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

274
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:57,280
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

275
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:03,740
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

276
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:08,410
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

277
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:30,510
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
